# UNERA V2 — Typography & Font Types

**Canonical implementation (copy patterns from here):** `NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html` — `@font-face` block, `--font-*` tokens, and Typography section pages (Typographic family, Primary typefaces English, Chinese, Arabic).

**Brand narrative (voice, trust, community context — not font metrics):** `Brand Guide/Brand Rationale UNERA.docx`. When typography choices affect tone, they should feel **clear, institutional, and human-centered** (readable grotesk; no decorative display faces).

**Scope:** New-brand HTML under `NewUnera/` only. Do not apply old-brand (Space Grotesk) stacks to these files.

---

## 1. Primary Latin — Brand Intent vs Repo Files

| Layer | Rule |
|--------|------|
| **Brand (guidelines copy)** | **Oakes Grotesk** is the official UNERA typeface — do not replace or mix with arbitrary families. Reference: [Oakes Grotesk](https://supply.family/shop/oakes-grotesk/) (linked from `brand-style-guide.html`). |
| **Weights (English)** | Light **300**, Regular **400**, Medium **500**, SemiBold **600**, Bold **700** — each with **normal and italic** styles. |
| **This repository (web)** | Use **`TestFoundersGrotesk`** via local **`@font-face`** from `Brand Guide/*.otf`, with **`'Oakes Grotesk'`** as the **fallback** in the stack so intent stays correct if Oakes is installed. |

```css
--font-display: 'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;
--font-body:    'TestFoundersGrotesk', 'Oakes Grotesk', sans-serif;
```

---

## 2. Required `@font-face` Set (all ten files)

**Mandatory:** Latin web fonts for UNERA V2 MUST use **only** these OTFs under `Brand Guide/` (repo-relative paths). Do not substitute other filenames or font files for new or updated NewUnera work — this reflects the latest brand guideline for TestFoundersGrotesk.

| From `NewUnera/*.html` | From repo root |
|------------------------|----------------|
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Light.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Light.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-LightItalic.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-LightItalic.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Regular.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Regular.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-RegularItalic.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-RegularItalic.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Medium.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Medium.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-MediumItalic.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-MediumItalic.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Semibold.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Semibold.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-SemiboldItalic.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-SemiboldItalic.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Bold.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-Bold.otf` |
| `../Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-BoldItalic.otf` | `Brand Guide/TestFoundersGrotesk-BoldItalic.otf` |

**Weight → CSS mapping** (same ten files):

| `font-weight` | `font-style` | File (basename) |
|----------------|--------------|-----------------|
| 300 | normal | `TestFoundersGrotesk-Light.otf` |
| 300 | italic | `TestFoundersGrotesk-LightItalic.otf` |
| 400 | normal | `TestFoundersGrotesk-Regular.otf` |
| 400 | italic | `TestFoundersGrotesk-RegularItalic.otf` |
| 500 | normal | `TestFoundersGrotesk-Medium.otf` |
| 500 | italic | `TestFoundersGrotesk-MediumItalic.otf` |
| 600 | normal | `TestFoundersGrotesk-Semibold.otf` |
| 600 | italic | `TestFoundersGrotesk-SemiboldItalic.otf` |
| 700 | normal | `TestFoundersGrotesk-Bold.otf` |
| 700 | italic | `TestFoundersGrotesk-BoldItalic.otf` |

Use `font-family: 'TestFoundersGrotesk';`, `format('opentype')`, and `font-display: swap` on every rule.

**No heavier Latin weight:** There is **no** 800/900 face. Do **not** use `font-weight: 800` or `900` on the primary Latin stack — use **700** (Bold) maximum; otherwise the browser synthesizes weight and typography drifts off-brand.

